7:   "why": "one control: the joystick sits on the side of the band, where the owner marked it; a long press on it records. The exterior has the joystick opening, the two microphone holes on the underside and the recording light's window; it exists for ring sizes US 7 to 13. On US 7 and US 8 the joystick sits a little lower on the band (84 and 81 degrees from the top, against 78 on US 9 to 13), so that the battery fits",
12:   "why": "the 3D inside model follows the exterior and its fit check passes at all seven ring sizes, US 7 to 13 (model v6.2, 48 or 49 parts by size). The battery, the motor and the cable slots have their own position per size; on US 7, 8 and 9 the motor pocket opens a small sealed window into the block. Two parts do not fit as drawn: the screen maker's cable is wider than its pocket, and the antenna's solder pads lie off the board. The charging pads are being moved 1.0 mm sideways to meet the case's pins",
37:   "why": "the charging case is the soft cube the owner chose (45.5 x 45.9 x 41.4 mm, 700 mAh battery): the ring lies flat around a centre post, the lid swivels aside, and the ring charges through pads on the inside of its band. An independent review found that the case's four pins stand 1.0 mm to one side of the ring's pads, so the case cannot charge the ring as drawn; the ring's pads are being moved onto the pin row. The case's fit check passed with the joystick at one angle for every size; the check with the lower joystick of US 7 and US 8 is in work, with a finish and detail pass on the look. The spring pin is a proposal, not confirmed",
295:The Centre column is the action of a short press of the centre (section 2.1) when the screen is on. Menu items in SCR_MENU, in this order: "Recordings", "Pair phone", "Settings", "Power off". Settings in SCR_SETTINGS, in this order: "Screen brightness" (3 levels), "Vibration" (on/off; off disables MH and joystick ticks only, never M1, M2, M3, MF, MW), "Time format" (24 h / 12 h), "About" (firmware version, serial).
335:- **One code path:** the function `rec_mics_on()` is the only code that enables VDD_MIC (section 4.5, start step 2). It first powers the screen if it is off (sequence of section 3.3) and draws the red dot and the timer at 00:00:00; it enables VDD_MIC only when the screen driver has accepted that frame (`display_write()` returned 0 and the display is not blanked). If it fails, VDD_MIC stays off and the row "long press of the joystick centre, recording sign not drawn" applies (section 1.2). The close turns VDD_MIC off before the screen may leave the recording pictures. Nothing in `RECORDING` blanks the screen or drives OLED_PWR_EN low: the screen-off timer, the lock of section 2.2 and the current-limit action of section 8.7 dim to SCR_REC_DIM instead.
754:Four modes. The plan's three (media, presenter, pointer) and a fourth, agent, from the owner's words of 2026-11-11: "You can even control claude code with it". The wearer picks the mode on the ring. Each joystick action on the mode's control screen sends this to the active device:
765:- A key goes out only for a real action of the wearer on the joystick (Apple's accessory rule), only while a control screen is shown, and only for these five actions.
884:Caveat, from architecture section 4 and 16.8: the main-chip, storage, radio and power-chip lines are estimates, not datasheet values, and bench test B2 replaces them; the microphone line is from the Knowles datasheet copy at its 2.4 MHz test clock, not at the ring's 1.280 MHz (section 10.5, item 6). The recording light is removed in v7 (architecture 17.30): the 4.0 mA of architecture 17.15 counted 1.5 mA for it, so without the light the computed recording figure is 4.1 - 1.5 = 2.6 mA [CALC] plus the always-lit red dot and timer of section 3.2, whose cost is a bench item on the new panel (architecture 17.30) with no number yet. The thresholds of 1.1 and the hours of this section stay computed at 4.1 mA, the figure of architecture 17.26, until that bench result and a restated architecture figure **[CHOICE]**; 4.1 mA no longer counts a light. It excludes the motor (section 3.1) and the screen. **Requirement P2 (10 hours of recording) is NOT met by this ring**: the owner chose thinness over hours on 2026-11-10 (architecture 17.5). In every state other than `RECORDING` the microphones are off.
